        "reflect": {
          "stage": "reflect",
          "report": "## Reflect Strategy\n\nOf 20 open review issues, observe classified 12 genuine, 6 not-worth-it, 1 exaggerated, 1 duplicate. After applying YAGNI and evaluating fix complexity vs value, I propose 3 execution clusters (10 issues) and 10 skips.\n\n### Recurring Patterns\n- **elegance dimensions** (low/mid/high): 5 open issues across 3 sub-dimensions. receiveMigration decomposition addresses low+mid elegance simultaneously. output barrel addresses high elegance.\n- **convention_outlier**: 2 open, both trivial renames. Batch together for one commit.\n- **cross_module_architecture**: 2 open / 1 recently resolved. Pattern of barrel bypasses and backwards dependencies \u2014 output module is the common thread.\n- **design_coherence**: 1 open / 3 recently resolved. Good progress, one remaining (receiveMigration) is highest-value single fix.\n- **logic_clarity**: 2 open / 1 recently resolved. Both are quick mechanical fixes.\n\n### Strategic Priorities\n1. receiveMigration decomposition \u2014 single fix improves design_coherence, low_level_elegance, and mid_level_elegance (3 dimensions).\n2. output module restructuring \u2014 barrel + dependency fix improves high_level_elegance and cross_module_architecture (2 dimensions).\n3. Quick mechanical fixes \u2014 5 trivial fixes across convention, logic, and contract dimensions.\n\n### Why Skip the Rest\n- not-worth-it issues (6): observe correctly identified these as over-engineering or pattern-appropriate. Decorator delegation is intentional SOLID. debug-level for best-effort IO is correct. settings descriptors are 4 entries with clear differences. findOrCreate is standard pattern. process() is standard strategy verb.\n- exaggerated (1): interaction_verification_coupling \u2014 tests verify behavioral outcomes through mocks, not pure interaction tests.\n- dual_path_token_resolution: works correctly, implicit contract is acceptable for 2-site coordination.\n- base_result_unsafe_downcast: low risk with 4 implementations, comment-level contract adequate.\n- output_formatter_test_gap: defer \u2014 per triage guidance, tests after code quality. Code quality fixes first.\n\n## Coverage Ledger\n- receive_migration_multi_responsibility -> cluster \"lifecycle-decomposition\"\n- receivemigration_monolith -> cluster \"lifecycle-decomposition\"\n- lifecycle_redundant_file_prefix -> cluster \"convention-renames\"\n- lifecycle_barrel_bypass -> cluster \"output-module-structure\"\n- output_missing_barrel_index -> cluster \"output-module-structure\"\n- output_depends_on_sync_for_formatting -> cluster \"output-module-structure\"\n- code_scanning_test_name_prefix -> cluster \"convention-renames\"\n- duplicate_deep_equal -> cluster \"quick-code-fixes\"\n- redundant_typeof_check_code_scanning -> cluster \"quick-code-fixes\"\n- repo_settings_diff_unchanged_omission -> cluster \"quick-code-fixes\"\n- authenticated_git_ops_18_pass_through_delegations -> skip \"not-worth-it-intentional-decorator-pattern\"\n- github_summary_debug_level_io_error -> skip \"not-worth-it-debug-appropriate-for-best-effort-io\"\n- settings_descriptor_repetition -> skip \"not-worth-it-4-entries-each-self-contained\"\n- settings_descriptor_glue_callbacks -> skip \"not-worth-it-overlaps-descriptor-repetition\"\n- findOrCreate_silent_mutation -> skip \"not-worth-it-standard-findOrCreate-pattern\"\n- generic_process_verb -> skip \"not-worth-it-standard-strategy-pattern-verb\"\n- interaction_verification_coupling -> skip \"exaggerated-tests-verify-behavioral-outcomes\"\n- dual_path_token_resolution -> skip \"genuine-but-low-value-implicit-contract-acceptable\"\n- base_result_unsafe_downcast -> skip \"genuine-but-low-risk-4-implementations-comment-contract\"\n- output_formatter_test_gap -> skip \"defer-tests-after-code-quality-fixes\"\n\n## Cluster Blueprint\nCluster \"lifecycle-decomposition\" (src/lifecycle/github-lifecycle-provider.ts)\n  - Decompose receiveMigration into 4 private helpers. Highest-value single refactor \u2014 improves design_coherence + low_level_elegance + mid_level_elegance simultaneously.\n  - Effort: medium. ~133 lines to restructure into orchestrator + helpers.\n  - Execute first \u2014 no dependencies on other clusters.\n\nCluster \"output-module-structure\" (src/output/, src/lifecycle/index.ts)\n  - Create output barrel index.ts, fix lifecycle barrel bypass, move formatDiffLine from sync/ to output/.\n  - Effort: small-medium. New file + import path updates across ~11 sites.\n  - Execute second \u2014 lifecycle barrel fix touches lifecycle/index.ts which lifecycle-decomposition also touches.\n  - Depends on: lifecycle-decomposition (to avoid merge conflicts in lifecycle/).\n\nCluster \"convention-renames\" (test/unit/settings/code-scanning/, src/lifecycle/)\n  - Rename code-scanning test files (remove domain prefix) and lifecycle module files (remove lifecycle- prefix).\n  - Effort: small. Mechanical renames + import updates.\n  - Execute third \u2014 lifecycle renames should happen after lifecycle-decomposition to avoid churn.\n  - Depends on: lifecycle-decomposition.\n\nCluster \"quick-code-fixes\" (src/settings/rulesets/diff.ts, src/config/validator.ts, src/settings/repo-settings/diff.ts)\n  - Remove duplicate deepEqual, simplify redundant typeof check, narrow RepoSettingsAction type.\n  - Effort: small. Three independent one-file fixes, no cross-dependencies.\n  - Execute in parallel with lifecycle-decomposition \u2014 no file overlap.\n\n## Execution Order\n1. quick-code-fixes (independent, trivial, immediate wins)\n2. lifecycle-decomposition (highest multi-dimension impact)\n3. output-module-structure (depends on lifecycle-decomposition)\n4. convention-renames (depends on lifecycle-decomposition)\n\n## Backlog Decisions\n- 179 unclustered items (mostly dead exports from barrel files): defer \u2014 these are mechanical findings that don't affect subjective scores. The 75% subjective weight means review issue fixes have 3x the score impact. After review clusters are complete, promote dead exports as a batch autofix.\n\n## Skip Decisions\nSkip \"not-worth-it-intentional-decorator-pattern\" \u2014 AuthenticatedGitOps delegation is standard Decorator for DI codebase. Proxy loses type safety.\nSkip \"not-worth-it-debug-appropriate-for-best-effort-io\" \u2014 debug level correct for cosmetic GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY write.\nSkip \"not-worth-it-4-entries-each-self-contained\" \u2014 4 descriptors differ in key/label/factory/callback. Data-driven saves ~30 lines at cost of indirection.\nSkip \"not-worth-it-overlaps-descriptor-repetition\" \u2014 same root as descriptor repetition, same judgment.\nSkip \"not-worth-it-standard-findOrCreate-pattern\" \u2014 universally recognized pattern name (ActiveRecord, Sequelize, Prisma).\nSkip \"not-worth-it-standard-strategy-pattern-verb\" \u2014 process() is standard Strategy method. Internal already uses applySettings.\nSkip \"exaggerated-tests-verify-behavioral-outcomes\" \u2014 observe confirmed tests check outcomes through mocks, not pure interaction verification.\nSkip \"genuine-but-low-value-implicit-contract-acceptable\" \u2014 dual token resolution works, 2-site coordination is manageable.\nSkip \"genuine-but-low-risk-4-implementations-comment-contract\" \u2014 baseResult cast serves 4 subtypes with optional fields only.\nSkip \"defer-tests-after-code-quality-fixes\" \u2014 per triage guidance: clean code first, test clean code.",
